1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
In this video, you'll learn the correct things to do as the roamer, if your team is losing.

2
00:00:04,839 --> 00:00:07,980
I've struggled through countless of games where the enemy had the advantage,

3
00:00:08,199 --> 00:00:09,400
so I'll tell you what I've learned.

4
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:14,519
Number 1, stick to the ally with the most gold or highest capability to turn the game around.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,739
This could be anyone, and only you can figure out who it is in your game.

6
00:00:19,179 --> 00:00:22,120
One way to do that is by checking the one with the highest farm,

7
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:25,839
best KDA, or who you believe can deal the most damage and follow-up.

8
00:00:27,039 --> 00:00:30,440
Number 2, don't try to contest the lord if you believe you can defend,

9
00:00:30,579 --> 00:00:32,380
or you have no chance of getting the lord.

10
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:37,719
For example, during the M5 knockout stage, where it was Onik versus AP Bren in game 1,

11
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:42,240
notice how Onik knew that it was too risky, where they were way too far behind in gold,

12
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:45,340
and instead decided to not contest the lord and just defend.

13
00:00:46,219 --> 00:00:50,320
The reason you shouldn't contest could either be because the enemy jungler has retribution

14
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:53,479
and your jungler is dead, or you don't have any allies with you.

15
00:00:54,219 --> 00:00:55,820
But when it comes to how you should defend,

16
00:00:55,840 --> 00:01:00,079
I want you to try to not let the enemy minion waves enter the attack range of your base,

17
00:01:00,219 --> 00:01:02,659
as the enemies then can ignore you and push your base.

18
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:06,180
Try to make the lord or enemy minions follow you,

19
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:10,340
so that you delay the enemies from pushing your base until your allies respawn if they're dead.

20
00:01:11,319 --> 00:01:15,000
Number 3, don't initiate on the enemy unless your team has enough damage.

21
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:19,420
This is about your team's items, where you ask yourself whether they have enough farm

22
00:01:19,420 --> 00:01:22,060
to actually deal damage when they follow up your initiation.

23
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:25,739
Even as a tank main, it's still a good idea to learn about

24
00:01:25,739 --> 00:01:29,180
the other role's items, so that you know when your allies reach their power spikes,

25
00:01:29,439 --> 00:01:31,900
which is when an item gives them a huge boost in damage.

26
00:01:32,439 --> 00:01:36,560
An item that gives a power spike in the late game are typically items with penetration,

27
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:38,980
which is the divine glaive and the malefic roar.

28
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:43,859
So if you feel like your allies don't deal enough damage, and the enemies are too tanky,

29
00:01:43,959 --> 00:01:47,340
it could be because your allies haven't gotten their penetration items yet to

30
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:48,980
reduce the enemy's defense stats.

31
00:01:49,939 --> 00:01:54,819
Number 4, if you haven't gotten all of your tank items yet, and you're still squishy, remember to

32
00:01:54,819 --> 00:01:58,760
be careful with your positioning, since the enemies have a lot of damage in the late game,

33
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:03,519
and can burst you down even if you're a tank. You should only be the front line for your team

34
00:02:03,519 --> 00:02:07,640
when necessary meaning when you absolutely can and won't get bursted down in seconds.

35
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,860
The reason you shouldn't all the time, is because sometimes your allies can avoid

36
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:14,680
the enemy's skills themselves and don't need you to shield them.

37
00:02:15,439 --> 00:02:20,360
Number 5, trade kills with the enemy whenever you can, but make sure your team is still able

38
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:24,800
to defend the turrets and base. This means that you sacrifice yourself to get killed.

39
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,719
иль키 너는 상대의 수수료가 나름 곤� classic림만 상장할 수 있거든.

40
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:29,979
when your team is behind in gold and it's clever because you actually gain more gold

41
00:02:29,979 --> 00:02:33,340
from killing an enemy compared to an enemy killing you or your allies.

42
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:37,080
The idea is so that your team can get their items faster to have

43
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:41,099
a higher chance of making a comeback. To make it less risky, because your allies

44
00:02:41,099 --> 00:02:44,740
will be alone while you're respawning, you should sacrifice yourself to take out the

45
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:48,819
big problem of the enemy team. That way they will have less chance of ending your base.

46
00:02:49,759 --> 00:02:54,740
Number 6, if you're in a situation where you've lost all of your turrets and you and your team want

47
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:59,520
to contest the Lord, make sure you don't initiate a teamfight while enemy minion waves are coming to

48
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:03,659
your base, because then your teammates need to clear the waves to stop the enemy from getting

49
00:03:03,659 --> 00:03:08,599
a chance to backdoor your base. This means that you must pay attention to when minion waves are

50
00:03:08,599 --> 00:03:12,879
coming, even when you can't see them when you look at the map, by checking whenever your own minion

51
00:03:12,879 --> 00:03:18,259
waves spawn. So if you do predict a minion wave will come, your teammate will eventually notice

52
00:03:18,259 --> 00:03:22,000
it too when they're revealed on the map, so that's where you should let them clear first,

53
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,979
before you engage. However, of course trying to steal the Lord and retreating immediately

54
00:03:26,979 --> 00:03:31,699
afterwards is different and okay, but a teamfight without your whole team is not a good idea.

55
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:36,919
The only time you can initiate a teamfight, despite there being minion waves on their way

56
00:03:36,919 --> 00:03:41,539
to your base, is when all the enemies are at Lord, unless they have a Ling or Fanny who can rotate

57
00:03:41,539 --> 00:03:48,460
fast. Number 7, Target the Enemy Carrying Their Team. After all the games I've played, I've come

58
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:51,879
to realize that there's usually only one enemy, that is the big problem,

59
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:57,280
and once that enemy is dead, the rest of the enemy team collapses. Normally, that would be

60
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:01,740
the enemy marksman in the late game, but it could as well be the tank or support of the enemy team,

61
00:04:01,939 --> 00:04:05,680
who's doing all the work by being the frontline, initiating huge teamfights,

62
00:04:05,879 --> 00:04:11,080
stunning your teammates and healing their allies. So if it is their tank who is the big problem,

63
00:04:11,259 --> 00:04:15,819
I suggest stunning him, the moment the enemy tank is out of positioning and away from his teammates,

64
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:21,139
but be sure your team will follow and attack. An example of a support who could be the biggest

65
00:04:21,139 --> 00:04:21,980
problem is S4. S4 is a tank that can be used to support your teammates, but if you're not

66
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,980
sure who it is, you can just use S4. If the enemy team heavily relies on his healing and you stun him

67
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:30,920
and they attack, then they'll collapse easier. Find out who's the biggest problem and focus on

68
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:36,300
that enemy, even if it's not enemy marksman, mage or jungler. You want to be able to spot

69
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:41,019
and predict that enemy on the map. To help you with that, you should watch this guide about map

70
00:04:41,019 --> 00:04:41,339
awareness.

